A stack in Python is a data structure that follows the LIFO principle — Last In, First Out.
This means the last element added to the stack is the first one removed.

Think of it like a stack of plates 🍽️:

You place a plate on top → push

You remove the top plate → pop
You cannot remove plates from the middle or bottom.

Basic Stack Operations
Operation	Meaning
push()	Add an element to the top
pop()	Remove the top element
peek() / top	View the top element without removing it
isEmpty()	Check if stack is empty
